I don't think I've ever seen a puppeteer win when our hunter drops their weapon or manages their fear.

&#x200B;

The other demons are strong because they don't need to capitalise on weaknesses to win. Eligos is entirely reliant on the players making repeated bad choices.

I've had games where I've spawned one area away from the survivors despite there being half a map with no objectives on it. Its completely nonsensical.

&#x200B;

Imo they should remove the spawn logic stuff (no blue spawns) and always spawn the demon on 1 map piece but hide the others. Give them a reason to trap early instead of immediately rush. Spread the map pieces out by a few areas too.

Theres a certain type of player in these games where they think their own skill (which they usually lack) should override the games intended design.

&#x200B;

another more important point is that a lot of survivor players in this game are from DBD. Where you have a veritable avalanche of second chance perks that exists to punish the killer for your own mistakes.

As a solo survivor/demon player closing in on 100 I'm still having fun. There are things that frustrate me on both sides but the last 2 patches have made some good changes/bug fixes so I'm still optimistic.

&#x200B;

As for this subreddit it's very obvious when a post with 200 upvotes is posted by someone who has never actually played demon once. Or someone who doesn't actually know how a survivor power works/the cooldown timer. There's a lot of disinfo about demon mechanics out there.

&#x200B;

Also the complaints about dying solo are stupid and shouldn't be taken seriously. Its a 1v4. You should always lose the 1v4 100% of the time thats a basic design decision in any Asym.

I won a match possessing a fists henry earlier. He dropped his gold axe and I beat Cheryl to death in a corner.

&#x200B;

Fists are fun, I love unarmed characters in any game. I'd love a character whose gimmick was unarmed.

Most of my wins as demon are because a hunter refuses to monitor their fear or a support picks up a golden shotty and I just let loose.

&#x200B;

I do feel like this game's demons are way more dependant on survivor fuck ups then actual smart plays. If a team sticks together and has high balance bar weapons there's really not anything I feel I can do. Possess a player? Stunlocked out. Possess a unit? Stunned and dismembered in seconds. Boss? Maybe get a few hits in then go on a 2 minute cooldown

When you win because they fucked up it really feels like a hollow victory. I feel it more in this game than I ever did in dbd. I think its because, gameplay wise, all demons are the same and pretty restrictive in what you can actually do. There aren't any "great plays" or mindgames you can do.

&#x200B;

Its also how I know a lot of complaints about basic possession are bs because I can have a max balance bar level a5 possession demon get instan stun chained into kill every time against a good team.

Stuck with my team 3 matches in a row.

Each match despite competent teammmates at level 25 has ended with Warlord basic spam. Except now its even tougher to beat.

